    {
      "id": "PR_kwDODjvEJM64nCJe",
      "title": "Add timeout to vm-runner",
      "author": "pauldowman",
      "number": 18594,
      "body": "<!--\r\nContributions welcome! See https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/.github/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md\r\n-->\r\n\r\n**Description**\r\nAdds a configurable timeout for VM execution in the run-trace command to prevent the runner from hanging indefinitely if the VM hangs.\r\n\r\nChanges:\r\n- Add --vm-timeout CLI flag to run-trace command with a default of 3 hours. Set to 0 to disable timeout.\r\n- Apply timeout context in runOnce() before creating the trace provider\r\n- ~~Add timeouts_total metric to track timeout occurrences~~ (removed)\r\n- ~~Logs timeout specifically (as opposed to panic or failure)~~(removed)\r\n\r\n\r\n**Tests**\r\n\r\n- `TestNewRunnerSetsTimeout` - verifies the timeout is stored in the Runner\r\n- `TestRunOnceAppliesTimeout` - verifies the context deadline is applied when timeout is set, and not applied when timeout is zero\r\n- `TestRunOnceReturnsTimeoutError` - verifies that a slow trace provider causes context.DeadlineExceeded to be returned\r\n\r\n**Additional context**\r\n\r\n**Metadata**\r\n\r\n<!-- \r\nInclude a link to any github issues that this may close in the following form:\r\n- Fixes #[Link to Issue]\r\n-->\r\n",
